  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for node `NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2` on run 3 of 6, with all 6 witnesses passing and all nine exception rules resolving.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_283_1d3_o2.lean`):\n- **When it judges:** the moment the signal turns to steady \"Don't Walk\", where at the observation before it was flashing with no countdown.\n- **Who it applies to:** a pedestrian who:\n  - last stepped from a sidewalk onto the roadway or lane while the signal showed \"Walk\" and they were facing it;\n  - was still on that roadway or lane at some point during the flashing phase.\n- **How far back it looks:** there is no time limit on finding that step. If the step happened before the recording started, the result is unknown.\n- **What it requires:** at that moment the pedestrian is no longer on the roadway or lane.\n- **Facing the signal:** written exactly as the node defines it, using the cosine and reach parameters.\n- **Readings of my own:** none were needed. The node's own reading (\"any place off the roadway counts as a place of safety\") is used as given.\n\n**The witnesses:** besides the five planned scenes (forbid, permit, idle, blind, history_boundary) I added `branch_1`. It's the forbid scene on a lane instead of a roadway, so the lane case is also tested.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **Run 1 failed:** three scenes came out unknown because one of the exception rules reads the roadway's direction of travel. I gave the roadway a direction at right angles to the crossing.\n2. **Run 2 failed:** on the roadway scenes an exception rule then applied and blocked this rule. It was probably the one for a pedestrian crossing outside a crosswalk; the lane scene still passed. I added a marked crosswalk along the pedestrian's path.\n3. **Run 3:** OK.\n\nBefore the first run, I also ran the gate command once with `--help` added. That wasn't allowed, so it was denied without running and didn't use any of the budget.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- task_result.md",
